# ⚠️ DEPRECATED — Vite mode files are now used instead.
#
#   .env.development.example  → copy to .env.development  (used by `npm run dev`)
#   .env.production.example   → copy to .env.production    (used by `npm run build`)
#
# Vite picks these up automatically based on mode — no --mode flag needed.
#
# ⚠️ VITE_* values are BAKED INTO THE BUNDLE at build time. Changing them
# requires a rebuild + redeploy, not a restart. Only the publishable key
# belongs in a browser bundle — never the Supabase secret key.
#
# In Cloudflare Pages the production values are set in the dashboard
# (Settings → Environment variables → Production); .env.production is for
# local production-parity builds.
